  intro: "Oklahoma City sits at the crossing of I-35, I-40, and I-44, making it a natural consolidation point and one of the less expensive places in the region to arrange a long-distance move. In Oklahoma we plan around two things unique to the state: an extremely active spring severe-weather season, and Tinker Air Force Base plus Fort Sill, which together generate substantial military relocation volume with fixed report dates.",
  migration: "Oklahoma has swung to modest net inbound in recent years, gaining households from Texas, California, and Colorado on cost of living. Oklahoma City's metro growth is the driver, with Edmond and Norman absorbing much of it. Tulsa has stabilized and actively recruits remote workers. Outbound flow still runs strongly to Texas, which remains the single largest destination for Oklahoma movers by a wide margin.",
